1
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,680
Where's the money?

2
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,840
Where's the money? I'm asking you, where is it?

3
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,280
I swear I don't have any left.

4
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,600
How dare you lie to me!

5
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,880
Where's my money?!

6
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Lying to me!

7
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,760
You lied to me!

8
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:50,640
How dare you lie to me!

9
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,880
Hiding my money!

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Go to hell!

11
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,760
Hand it over!

12
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,880
The money!

13
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,880
Give it to me!

14
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,000
Hand it over!

15
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,320
You're asking for it!

16
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,240
How dare you bite me!

17
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,520
Take this!

18
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:09,800
Take that!

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,600
And that!

20
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,760
Get off!

21
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,760
Take that!

22
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,800
You hit me?

23
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,520
Screw you!

24
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,360
Bite me! Go on, bite me!

25
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:29,880
Bite me!

26
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,640
How dare you bite me!

27
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,120
At least eat a few bites.

28
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,560
I know you're hurting,

29
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,520
but your health comes first.

30
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,840
Auntie Tang wouldn't want to see you like this.

31
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,600
Sometimes,

32
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,960
people force your hand,

33
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,560
circumstances push you,

34
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,160
and a whole lifetime

35
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,120
is decided just like that.

36
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,440
Can you

37
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,280
tell me about Auntie Tang?

38
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,960
Hongyu had a hard life.

39
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:19,400
When she was little,

40
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,240
there were many kids in her family.

41
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,160
She got married very young.

42
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,120
The man she married

43
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,440
didn't lift a finger.

44
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:33,960
She was treated like a maid.

45
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:35,240
Right after having her baby,

46
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,720
before her first month was even up,

47
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,880
she had to get back to work.

48
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:41,800
It was so tragic.

49
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,440
Then how did she end up in prison?

50
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,840
That man of hers,

51
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,480
whenever he had too much to drink,

52
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,600
he'd beat her up.

53
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,840
You only saw the scar on her face.

54
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,760
You didn't see the ones on her body.

55
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:09,360
Those scars were the truly heartbreaking ones.

56
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:11,800
Where's the money?

57
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,040
Give me the money now!

58
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,080
Hualin's grandma took it.

59
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,480
Why would my mom take money from you?

60
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,000
Where is it?

61
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:24,440
It's really gone.

62
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:25,600
I've worked hard all day.

63
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,040
You'd better serve me well.

64
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,600
What are you doing?!

65
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:32,920
Give it to me!

66
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,680
I really don't have it!

67
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,840
Don't hit my mom!

68
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,280
Get out!

69
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:41,120
Let go of my mom!

70
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,280
Hualin!

71
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,360
You let go of my mom!

72
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,160
Let go of her!

73
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,880
Stay still.

74
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:56,680
Screw you!

75
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,280
I told you to stay still!

76
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,440
She thought about running away,

77
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,080
and getting a divorce.

78
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,280
But for the sake of her child,

79
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,320
she chose to stay.

80
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,760
Mom, does it hurt?

81
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,200
It doesn't hurt, sweetie.

82
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,680
Dad was just drunk.

83
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,120
He'll be fine when he sobers up.

84
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,680
She said, one night,

85
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,800
that son of a bitch got dead drunk again.

86
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:47,960
Where's the money?

87
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,040
As soon as he walked in,

88
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,760
he started beating Hongyu.

89
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:51,920
You dare lie to me?

90
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,920
Hiding my money?

91
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,480
Die!

92
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,280
Beating Hongyu wasn't enough for him.

93
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,320
He went after Hualin too.

94
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,080
As for Hongyu,

95
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,320
she couldn't let Hualin suffer.

96
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,600
So she picked up a hammer.

97
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,120
Bite me, will you?!

98
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,320
By the time she came to her senses,

99
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:15,120
that son of a bitch was dead.

100
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,360
Hongyu was terrified.

101
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,120
Her mind went completely blank.

102
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,760
Then she turned herself in.

103
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,360
How tragic.

104
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,560
She spent 12 years in there.

105
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,200
While she was in prison,

106
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,520
she always told me

107
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,360
that after getting out,

108
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,960
she'd make it up to Hualin.

109
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,560
See him start a family,

110
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,400
and really be there for him.

111
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,680
Life was so unfair to her.

112
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,320
I hope

113
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,520
she won't suffer like this in heaven.

114
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,800
When you first got out of prison,

115
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,200
Director Ma from the sub-district office told me

116
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,240
that many newly released inmates

117
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,000
can't adapt to the outside world.

118
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,120
They either go right back in,

119
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,320
or

120
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,640
choose suicide.

121
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,400
So you stayed

122
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:30,440
and gave me all these crappy jobs

123
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:32,880
because you were afraid I'd kill myself?

124
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:38,960
I was.

125
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,200
What's there to be afraid of?

126
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,720
I don't dwell on things.

127
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,400
I won't do anything foolish.

128
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,520
Besides,

129
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,720
I've still got you, right?

130
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,640
Auntie Tang had Chu Hualin too,

131
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,960
but she still couldn't see a way out.

132
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,400
What on earth was she thinking?

133
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,200
I just don't get it.

134
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:14,360
Why couldn't she see a way out? Why take this path?

135
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,000
That night,

136
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,600
What's wrong?

137
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,440
It's nothing.

138
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:27,240
Guess it's just old age.

139
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,600
The wind makes my eyes water.

140
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,480
She said the wind made her eyes water.

141
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:36,320
I really thought it was just the wind!

142
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,160
She kept talking

143
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:44,200
about everything she went through in life.

144
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,280
Sister Lan,

145
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,960
having these few happy days,

146
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,680
means my life hasn't been in vain.

147
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,280
Meeting you in this lifetime

148
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,400
makes it all worth it.

149
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:57,400
Why didn't I notice anything wrong with her?

150
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,680
If only I had

151
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,840
noticed that she

152
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,840
was feeling down

153
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,920
and couldn't see a way out,

154
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
if I had comforted her a bit more,

155
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,560
and talked to her more,

156
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,400
maybe she wouldn't have taken this path?

157
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,120
Stop blaming yourself.

158
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,440
I'll go find out what happened.

159
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,280
I hope Auntie Tang

160
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,640
can rest in peace up there.

161
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,840
When Auntie Tang was young,

162
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,120
she was really beautiful.

163
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,800
Yiran,

164
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,000
why do you think

165
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,520
Auntie Tang's death

166
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,640
is connected to Chu Hualin?

167
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,040
Because...

168
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,960
I know all too well how a child facing

169
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:11,200
a newly released mother they haven't seen in years

170
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,360
would react.

171
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,600
Hualin.

172
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,600
Have you been doing well these past few years?

173
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,600
Have Grandpa and Grandma been good to you?

174
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:45,960
Pretty good.

175
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:54,240
I...

176
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,280
I have evening classes at school.

177
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,960
Eat before you go.

178
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,760
I'll go cook.

179
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,480
It'll be ready soon.

180
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,600
I remember you love sweet and sour ribs.

181
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,320
I'll go to the market for some groceries in a bit.

182
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:32,880
No need.

183
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,760
I'm going to eat at Grandpa and Grandma's.

184
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,560
Their place is closer to school.

185
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,440
Since I'm back now,

186
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:45,360
let's not bother Grandpa and Grandma.

187
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,720
Dinner will be ready soon.

188
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,440
I don't want to eat.

189
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,240
What about the weekend?

190
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,320
Are you coming back for the weekend?

191
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,360
No.

192
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,920
Hualin.

193
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,560
Murderer.

194
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,960
Hualin.

195
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,800
Come home with me.

196
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,120
What are you doing here?

197
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,800
Mom made sweet and sour ribs for you.

198
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,760
And some snacks.

199
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:53,560
Take them back with you.

200
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:54,280
I don't want them.

201
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:55,680
Hualin,

202
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:57,400
you study so hard.

203
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,840
Don't touch me!

204
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,400
Can you stop coming to see me?

205
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:06,080
What did Mom do wrong?

206
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:07,760
Come home with me.

207
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:10,960
His mom is a murderer, right?

208
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,880
That's terrifying.

209
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:12,840
Oh my god.

210
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,200
That's her.

211
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:18,040
Do you know what they call me at school?

212
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,960
They say I'm a murderer's son.

213
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,200
The spawn of an ex-con.

214
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,760
I work so hard at school,

215
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,000
trying to prove myself.

216
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,040
But because of you,

217
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,000
I don't even have a chance to achieve my dreams.

218
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,840
Grandma and Grandpa hate you too.

219
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,760
Because you killed their only son.

220
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:34,960
You killed my dad.

221
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,080
My life is ruined because of you.

222
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:43,920
Hualin...

223
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,640
Mom was wrong.

224
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,440
I'm begging you.

225
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,360
Don't come looking for me anymore.

226
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,280
Just leave me alone.

227
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:58,440
I never want to see you again.

228
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,520
Hualin

229
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,360
These are the letters I wrote to Hualin over the years.

230
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,560
He hasn't read a single one.

231
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,320
Yiran,

232
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,920
did you know?

233
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,480
When Hualin was little,

234
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,760
he was like my little shadow,

235
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:24,040
clinging to me all day long.

236
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:29,800
Every night at bedtime, I had to hold him.

237
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:32,240
Kissing him, cuddling him.

238
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,920
He'd tell me absolutely everything.

239
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,960
I don't hate his grandparents.

240
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,800
I'm the one who killed their son.

241
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
It's just fate.

242
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,840
His grandparents made him hate me.

243
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,920
But I don't hate them for it.

244
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:12,000
Tell me, why is it that people,

245
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:16,200
especially those closest to us,

246
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:21,600
have to take the long way around

247
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,520
just to realize that in each other's hearts,

248
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:26,320
they're the most important one?

249
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,440
Sister Lan asked me the other day

250
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,720
what I wished for at the temple.

251
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:49,120
What else could I wish for?

252
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,440
I just hope

253
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:55,040
Hualin grows up safe and sound,

254
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:58,080
gets married and has kids,

255
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,080
settles down and builds a career,

256
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:02,280
and stays free from illness and misfortune.

257
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,440
Yiran,

258
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,200
I know

259
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,960
a mother like me

260
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,320
is just holding him back.

261
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,120
No, no.

262
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:38,520
I also know

263
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:42,320
that if I weren't around,

264
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:47,880
he'd be better off.

265
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:51,320
That's not true, Auntie Tang.

266
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,480
It's not.

267
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:03,080
Auntie Tang! Auntie Tang!

268
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:04,120
Auntie Tang!

269
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:43,560
I actually used to yell right in Wu Huilian's face,

270
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,760
accusing her of getting my Pops killed.

271
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,160
I also told her

272
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,360
she wasn't fit to be a mother.

273
00:21:58,760 --> 00:21:59,480
Looking back now,

274
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,440
how am I any different from Chu Hualin?

275
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:07,600
We both say the cruelest things

276
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,440
to the people who love us most.

277
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,600
But I truly hated her back then.

278
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,600
Hated her for being so impulsive.

279
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,880
Hated her for acting so self-righteous.

280
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:24,360
Hated her for leaving me with so much trauma.

281
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,440
It took me a long time to realize

282
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,520
that she actually did nothing wrong.

283
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:37,040
Just like Auntie Tang,

284
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,160
she simply acted in the moment,

285
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,920
making a subconscious choice.

286
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,080
A choice made

287
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:47,040
with no time to judge right from wrong,

288
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:52,440
and no way to foresee the cost.

289
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,280
Yiran,

290
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,000
you're not like Chu Hualin.

291
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:06,000
Aren't we both ungrateful wretches?

292
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,200
You feel regret.

293
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,120
You reflect on things.

294
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:10,240
But Chu Hualin...

295
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,520
Auntie Tang used her life to try and change him,

296
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,760
yet he still hasn't realized

297
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:17,360
how much Auntie Tang loved him.

298
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,600
In this life,

299
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:20,840
everyone has regrets.

300
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:22,400
Everyone makes mistakes.

301
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:25,160
Since the past cannot be undone,

302
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,400
we should cherish the present.

303
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:28,720
But some words, once spoken,

304
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,760
are like throwing acid.

305
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,440
Even if the other person forgives you,

306
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,640
the scars will still be there.

307
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,000
Mothers

308
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,960
will never blame their own children.

309
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,320
They only blame themselves

310
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:46,280
for not giving their children enough.

311
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:50,320
Auntie Lan definitely never blamed you either.

312
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:52,880
Look,

313
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:54,520
even in death, Auntie Tang's

314
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:58,200
biggest concern was her son.

315
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,000
Look at all things in this world.

316
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,840
Every year, they endure

317
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:10,640
wind, frost, rain, and snow,

318
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:12,600
which eventually leave scars.

319
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:14,160
But when the next year comes,

320
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,760
they are reborn

321
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,200
and bloom just the same.

322
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:26,960
So,

323
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,360
people with scars need to be reborn too.

324
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:34,680
Of course.

325
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:36,760
With love,

326
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:38,800
with time, and with action.

327
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:41,280
Auntie Tang didn't live to see it,

328
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:42,520
but you're different.

329
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:44,000
You still have time

330
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:45,280
to work together with Auntie Lan

331
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:47,160
and mend the rift between you two.

332
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:56,800
Chen Baixi,

333
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:00,800
you really shouldn't be an actor.

334
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:03,800
Why?

335
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:06,160
You were born for the funeral business.

336
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:08,920
Chosen by heaven.

337
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,240
Chu Hualin.

338
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:40,200
We brought you Auntie Tang's belongings.

339
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:43,160
And Auntie Tang's funeral

340
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,000
is on Wednesday.

341
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,600
I don't want these things.

342
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,640
I'm not going to her funeral.

343
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:48,880
She's your own mother.

344
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:50,960
Are you really not going to see her one last time?

345
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:52,440
I don't have a mother.

346
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:54,920
Chu Hualin.

347
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:58,200
Do you know why she killed herself?

348
00:25:58,600 --> 00:25:59,960
Because of you.

349
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,640
Because you, her only son,

350
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:02,680
refused to acknowledge her.

351
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,480
She killed my dad.

352
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,400
She made me the son of a murderer.

353
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:07,800
Because of her, I can never hold my head high.

354
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,240
Why did she kill your dad?

355
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:14,400
Have you completely forgotten how your dad treated you both?

356
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:16,160
If you've forgotten,

357
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,640
I'll help you remember.

358
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:19,760
The scar on your mother's face...

359
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:20,840
how did she get it?

360
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,080
Give me the money!

361
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:30,320
You're asking for it!

362
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:36,760
How dare you bite me!

363
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:53,160
I've been living with my grandparents all these years.

364
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:54,720
They spent every day in tears.

365
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:56,560
They said she killed my dad on purpose.

366
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:58,040
How do you still not get it?

367
00:26:58,040 --> 00:26:59,880
That's because your mom killed their son.

368
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:01,120
That's why they made you hate her.

369
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:10,480
For over a decade,

370
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:14,000
she wrote you so many letters.

371
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:17,600
Because you never opened a single one,

372
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:20,040
do you know how heartbroken she was?

373
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:37,200
Did you not know about these letters,

374
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:41,000
or were you too afraid to read them?

375
00:28:19,040 --> 00:28:20,440
Do you think he'll read it?

376
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,200
I think he will.

377
00:28:24,080 --> 00:28:25,040
He definitely will.

378
00:29:54,640 --> 00:29:56,120
Hongyu.

379
00:29:58,480 --> 00:30:00,320
The path might be a bit dark

380
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,400
and not very easy to walk,

381
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:05,800
but it's still better than

382
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:07,760
suffering in this world.

383
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,280
Since you're all alone

384
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:11,760
down there,

385
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:13,680
take good care of yourself.

386
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:16,680
Eat whatever you want.

387
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:18,760
Go for a stroll

388
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,240
wherever you feel like it.

389
00:30:21,880 --> 00:30:23,840
If you meet the right person,

390
00:30:23,840 --> 00:30:25,360
someone who truly cares for you,

391
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:27,400
then spend your days together.

392
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:29,600
If you don't,

393
00:30:30,560 --> 00:30:31,480
being on your own

394
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:34,280
and living carefree is nice too, right?

395
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:42,280
I'll see you again sooner or later.

396
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,280
Wait for me.

397
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:01,080
I'll miss you.

398
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:31,080
Auntie Tang,

399
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,880
may the wishes you leave behind in this world

400
00:31:33,880 --> 00:31:34,800
all come true.

401
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:36,840
Please rest in peace.

402
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:50,680
Let's go.

403
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,360
Mom.

404
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:36,000
I read all your letters.

405
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:40,360
I'm sorry.

406
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:43,160
Have you ever wondered

407
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:46,880
if, when you got out of prison,

408
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,720
I hadn't come back,

409
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:49,800
what you would have done?

410
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:55,440
There are no "ifs" in this world.

411
00:33:56,280 --> 00:33:57,720
If there were,

412
00:33:58,360 --> 00:34:00,200
I wish that thing eight years ago

413
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:01,440
had never happened.

414
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:05,200
If only nothing had happened that day.

415
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:13,360
My whole life,

416
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:17,080
I've never been able to help you.

417
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:20,000
It's a good thing you're capable.

418
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:22,840
You've always relied on yourself.

419
00:34:23,160 --> 00:34:25,280
I really owe you too much.

420
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:33,800
You don't owe me anything.

421
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:37,520
Ever since I can remember,

422
00:34:37,520 --> 00:34:39,480
you haven't exactly been a good mother,

423
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:42,120
but you are Wu Huilian.

424
00:34:44,200 --> 00:34:46,240
You are the world's

425
00:34:46,720 --> 00:34:47,800
one and only

426
00:34:48,240 --> 00:34:49,360
Wu Huilian.

427
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:01,240
I'm sorry.

428
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:03,720
There's no need to be sorry.

429
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:08,600
You were just being true to yourself.

430
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:11,520
What's wrong with that?

431
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,160
I know

432
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:18,000
you did all this to make it up to me.

433
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:22,280
You wanted to give me everything you thought was best.

434
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:29,960
But it was your first time being a mom, too.

435
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:34,480
You had me at twenty-two,

436
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:39,920
and gave your best years,

437
00:35:40,600 --> 00:35:42,720
your most vibrant youth, all to me.

438
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:51,400
So you didn't let me down.

439
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:55,440
You only let yourself down a little.

440
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:01,480
Let's just

441
00:36:02,040 --> 00:36:03,200
call it even.

442
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,280
Let's both look forward.

443
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:13,040
You need to have your own life,

444
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:16,520
and I need to have mine.

445
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:19,200
From now on,

446
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:25,240
let's both just be ourselves.

447
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,160
Okay?

448
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:55,120
Okay.

449
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:16,960
Honey.

450
00:37:23,520 --> 00:37:24,200
Bye.

451
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:25,000
Bye.

452
00:37:25,640 --> 00:37:26,520
Be careful on your way to work.

453
00:37:26,520 --> 00:37:27,240
Okay.

454
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:29,000
Love,

455
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:31,000
perhaps in my heart,

456
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,720
has not completely faded away.

457
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:35,200
I just hope it

458
00:37:35,200 --> 00:37:36,600
won't bother you again.

459
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:37,760
Someone else

460
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:41,240
will love you just as I do.

461
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:08,600
You look so pretty, miss.

462
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:09,960
Your face is so petite!

463
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:11,000
Thanks. Thank you, sis.

464
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:14,160
Hey, handsome.

465
00:38:14,160 --> 00:38:14,600
Here.

466
00:38:14,600 --> 00:38:15,760
Put these sunglasses on.

467
00:38:16,080 --> 00:38:17,640
You look so handsome like this! So handsome!

468
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:20,800
Welcome!

469
00:38:21,680 --> 00:38:22,800
Are you two looking for a wedding dress?

470
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:23,880
Yes, yes. We're just taking a look.

471
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:24,560
Sure, sure.

472
00:38:24,560 --> 00:38:26,320
Come, right this way, please. This way.

473
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:29,720
Look, we have a lot of wedding dress styles here.

474
00:38:29,720 --> 00:38:30,960
You have such fair skin, miss.

475
00:38:30,960 --> 00:38:33,440
You'll definitely look gorgeous in this white one.

476
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:35,680
Look.

477
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:37,400
This one has pearls all over it.

478
00:38:37,760 --> 00:38:38,560
See?

479
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:39,720
Is this all you have?

480
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:40,400
Have a seat first.

481
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:40,840
Okay.

482
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:41,680
Just a moment.

483
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:45,600
Add extra potatoes.

484
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,040
Sure thing.

485
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:46,720
Coming right up!

486
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:14,800
Mr. Du,

487
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:16,560
rest in peace.

488
00:39:32,360 --> 00:39:37,320
Summer, summer quietly passed by, leaving little secrets.

489
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:40,760
I'll be just fine.

490
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:43,680
The flowers will smell sweet.

491
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:46,080
Frying eggs, frying eggs.

492
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:48,880
Let me fry a little egg.

493
00:39:57,040 --> 00:39:57,880
Mom!

494
00:39:57,880 --> 00:39:59,200
I'll be just...

495
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,320
Mom!

496
00:40:07,040 --> 00:40:08,560
I've told you so many times.

497
00:40:08,560 --> 00:40:10,200
Don't run the water when I'm showering.

498
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:10,960
When you use the water like that,

499
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:12,320
it goes hot and cold in here.

500
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,520
How am I supposed to shower?

501
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,160
What did you just call me?

502
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:29,240
What?

503
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:31,960
What's gotten into you?

504
00:40:33,120 --> 00:40:34,360
Say it again.

505
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:37,080
Mom.

506
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:40,880
Say it again.

507
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,560
Mom.

508
00:40:45,120 --> 00:40:46,200
I'm so happy! So happy!

509
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:47,320
So happy! So happy!

510
00:40:47,440 --> 00:40:47,960
The hat. The hat.

511
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:49,000
The hat. The hat. The hat.

512
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,640
You're so sweet, my darling.

513
00:40:53,640 --> 00:40:54,840
What's that smell?

514
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:55,640
What smell?

515
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:58,760
Oh no.

516
00:40:58,760 --> 00:40:59,480
My eggs!

517
00:40:59,480 --> 00:41:00,520
The eggs are burnt!

518
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:01,480
Oh no. Oh no.

519
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:03,080
My eggs are burnt.

520
00:41:07,520 --> 00:41:08,640
Sweetie.

521
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:09,920
Hurry up and wash.

522
00:41:09,920 --> 00:41:10,960
I promise.

523
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,320
I won't leave the water running again.

524
00:41:15,160 --> 00:41:15,960
Go on.

525
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:26,200
Mom!

526
00:41:27,680 --> 00:41:28,600
Mom!

527
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:32,680
Wang Daren!

528
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:33,760
Wang Daren!

529
00:41:33,760 --> 00:41:35,080
What's all the fuss about?

530
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:36,760
Did you win the lottery?

531
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,720
Even better than winning the lottery.

532
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:43,360
You're being so mysterious.

533
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:44,840
What's going on?

534
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,000
Yiran called me Mom.

535
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:47,440
Yiran called me Mom!

536
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:51,960
Really?

537
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:55,880
That's great!

538
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:57,600
Great!

539
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:00,280
I've waited for this day for so long.

540
00:42:00,520 --> 00:42:01,840
She finally called me Mom.

541
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:02,760
Wu Huilian.

542
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,560
You left the key in the door again.

543
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,040
You're always so forgetful.

544
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:07,600
You forgot your bag.

545
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:08,280
And your water bottle.

546
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:09,440
You always make me worry.

547
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:11,080
Uncle Daren, I'm leaving.

548
00:42:13,320 --> 00:42:15,400
I just love having my Yiran keep me in line.

549
00:42:17,160 --> 00:42:18,040
Brother Ming.

550
00:42:18,040 --> 00:42:18,720
Oh, Brother Ming.

551
00:42:18,720 --> 00:42:19,960
Did you hear that?

552
00:42:20,680 --> 00:42:23,440
Yiran just called Huilian Mom.

553
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:26,440
She called you Mom!

554
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:33,240
Yiran.

555
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:35,520
We'll leave in half an hour.

556
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:36,600
Okay.

557
00:42:43,080 --> 00:42:44,040
By the way.

558
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:46,240
Has the family read the eulogy I wrote?

559
00:42:46,240 --> 00:42:48,440
After the two sons of the Li family read it,

560
00:42:48,440 --> 00:42:50,480
they cried their eyes out.

561
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:51,560
They said

562
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:54,040
they lived with their father for nearly fifty years.

563
00:42:54,200 --> 00:42:55,840
They argued and they laughed.

564
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:58,360
But they never looked at their father

565
00:42:58,360 --> 00:43:00,040
from the perspective you described.

566
00:43:00,040 --> 00:43:01,920
They're very grateful to you.

567
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:04,120
You helped them know their father all over again.

568
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:06,800
Pops.

569
00:43:07,080 --> 00:43:07,640
Look.

570
00:43:07,640 --> 00:43:09,680
This is the pennant Grandpa Wang's son sent over.

571
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,120
What is it?

572
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:17,640
Good.

573
00:43:17,640 --> 00:43:18,880
That's good. That's good.

574
00:43:20,880 --> 00:43:22,520
This shows that

575
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:26,080
the client is very satisfied with our service.

576
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:29,360
As long as you do your job well,

577
00:43:29,360 --> 00:43:31,000
that's better than anything.

578
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:33,120
